Support screen.orientation.lock() and report the real rotation.

ScreenOrientationDelegateOhos (overlay, chrome/browser/ui/ohos) sets the app
window's preferred orientation through the engine HAR; it is installed by the
runtime bridge at browser start.

OhosScreen (overlay) now reports the display manager's rotation as the panel
rotation. It had reported 0 always, so screen.orientation.angle never moved
and a lock to a *-secondary orientation never resolved. With a rotation that
means what Android's does, ScreenInfo takes the mobile orientation type and
skips the Aura 90/270 swap, which exists for desktop panels.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

